Article 3 (Procedures for Project Evaluation, etc.)
(1) A project evaluation under Article 9 (2) of the Act shall be conducted in the following order:
1. Establishment of an evaluation plan;
2. Notification of the evaluation schedule and methods;
3. Documentary review and on-site inspection (including interviews with relevant persons);
4. Notification of the evaluation results;
5. Submission of opinions on the evaluation results and notification of the results of reviewing the submitted opinions;
6. Analysis of the evaluation results;
7. Public disclosure of the evaluation results.
(2) Where a non-profit, non-governmental organization that has been notified of evaluation results under paragraph (1) 4 intends to submit opinions on those results under paragraph (1) 5, it shall submit those opinions to the Minister of the Interior and Safety, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a special-case city within 20 days after receiving the notification of the evaluation results. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2017; May 1, 2023>
(3) Where a non-profit, non-governmental organization submits opinions pursuant to paragraphs (1) 5 and (2), the Minister of the Interior and Safety, a Mayor/Do Governor, or the head of a special-case city shall notify the organization of the results of reviewing those opinions within 60 days after receiving them. <Amended on Jul. 26, 2017; May 1, 2023>
